    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_d7qMiMtKwcN5RL8",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID6",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "Instructions For each question, you will see: one picture one sentence ending in a critical final...",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<h1><span style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:19px;\">Instructions</span></strong></span></h1>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">For each question, you will see: </span></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><span style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">one picture </span></span></li>\n\t<li><span style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">one sentence ending in a critical final word</span></span></li>\n</ul>\n<span style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Y</span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">our task is to judge <strong>how compatible the sentence's final word is with the situation shown in the picture</strong>.<br>\n<br>\nWhen making your judgment: </span></span>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><span style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><strong>Focus on the final word of the sentence. </strong>Treat the rest of the sentence as given. </span></span></li>\n\t<li><span style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">The picture does <strong>not</strong> need to prove that the sentence ending is the only possible interpretation. Simply, decide whether the final word is a <strong>natural and reasonable</strong> interpretation of the picture. </span></span></li>\n\t<li><span style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Please rely on your immediate, common-sense impression rather than overthinking each item. </span></span></li>\n</ul>\n<span style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Use the following rating scale:</span></span>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li><span style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><strong>Not compatible at all.&nbsp;</strong>The final word is clearly inconsistent with / unrelated to / contradicts the picture.</span></span></li>\n\t<li><span style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><strong>Low compatibility.&nbsp;</strong>The final word is technically plausible but would not be commonly associated with the picture / it would be unusual or difficult to reconcile this sentence with the picture.</span></span></li>\n\t<li><span style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><strong>Uncertain.</strong>&nbsp;The final word provides weak / ambiguous / mixed evidence for the picture.</span></span></li>\n\t<li><span style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><strong>Compatible.</strong>&nbsp;The final word makes the sentence a reasonable interpretation of the picture.</span></span></li>\n\t<li><span style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><strong>Very compatible.</strong>&nbsp;The final word makes the sentence very consistent with / a natural interpretation of the picture.</span></span></li>\n</ol>\n<span style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">The following is an example of the type of questions on this survey.&nbsp;</span></span>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "DataExportTag": "Q6",
        "QuestionType": "DB",
        "Selector": "TB",
        "DataVisibility": {
          "Private": false,
          "Hidden": false
        },
        "Configuration": {
          "QuestionDescriptionOption": "UseText"
        },
        "QuestionDescription": "Instructions For each question, you will see: one picture one sentence ending in a critical final...",
        "ChoiceOrder": [
